1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,277
You found the perfect part online:

2
00:00:02,277 --> 00:00:04,562
a phone stand for the wall, free to download.

3
00:00:04,562 --> 00:00:05,832
There's just one problem.

4
00:00:05,832 --> 00:00:07,000
Your phone doesn't fit.

5
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,224
And an STL file can't really be edited.

6
00:00:10,224 --> 00:00:12,230
It's just a shell of triangles.

7
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:19,207
Today, an AI agent turns that STL into a real, adjustable model, and then we make it fit.

8
00:00:19,207 --> 00:00:20,900
No CAD knowledge needed.

9
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:22,569
We use SOMA.

10
00:00:22,569 --> 00:00:26,799
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

11
00:00:28,149 --> 00:00:29,240
Here is the part:

12
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:33,799
a wall-mounted phone stand by High Desert Hacker, shared on Printables.

13
00:00:36,349 --> 00:00:38,786
The description gives the limit:

14
00:00:38,786 --> 00:00:43,889
phones up to 3.25 inches wide and 0.56 inches thick, with the case.

15
00:00:43,889 --> 00:00:46,479
That's about 83 by 14 millimeters.

16
00:00:47,179 --> 00:00:51,638
My phone, in its rugged case, is 90 millimeters wide and 18 thick.

17
00:00:51,638 --> 00:00:52,989
It simply won't fit.

18
00:00:53,689 --> 00:00:56,612
The license is Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike.

19
00:00:56,612 --> 00:01:01,819
So we may change it, as long as we credit the author and share our version under the same license.

20
00:01:02,519 --> 00:01:04,249
We download the STL file.

21
00:01:05,616 --> 00:01:09,739
In SOMA, we start a new model, click Import, and pick the downloaded file.

22
00:01:09,739 --> 00:01:13,026
It goes into the inputs folder, where the agent can use it.

23
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:17,893
Click the STL, and SOMA shows it in the viewer.

24
00:01:18,593 --> 00:01:22,305
But switch on the wireframe, and you see what an STL really is:

25
00:01:22,305 --> 00:01:23,778
a mesh of flat triangles.

26
00:01:23,778 --> 00:01:27,843
There's no width to change and no wall thickness, just corner points.

27
00:01:29,049 --> 00:01:32,379
So instead of pushing triangles around, we let the agent rebuild it.

28
00:01:33,629 --> 00:01:37,679
On the right, we start Claude Code, our agent, right inside the model folder.

29
00:01:40,096 --> 00:01:43,022
Then we simply say what we want, in plain words:

30
00:01:43,022 --> 00:01:48,386
rebuild the STL as a parametric model, and keep the original as a see-through reference.

31
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:55,741
The agent reads the mesh with a few lines of Python, measures the plates, ribs and cutouts, and writes them as CadQuery code.

32
00:01:55,741 --> 00:01:59,090
Every time the code changes, SOMA builds the model and shows it.

33
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,977
Here's the result:

34
00:02:00,977 --> 00:02:03,250
a real solid model, built from code.

35
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:07,203
The original STL sits in the same place, see-through.

36
00:02:07,203 --> 00:02:08,615
Hide it, show it again:

37
00:02:08,615 --> 00:02:10,640
the rebuild matches the download.

38
00:02:11,890 --> 00:02:14,932
The agent also turned the important sizes into parameters.

39
00:02:14,932 --> 00:02:16,820
You find them in the Parameters tab.

40
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:21,181
Drag a slider, and the model rebuilds within seconds.

41
00:02:21,181 --> 00:02:24,014
Here the width, and here the ledge depth:

42
00:02:24,014 --> 00:02:26,086
the slot that holds the phone.

43
00:02:26,086 --> 00:02:27,330
No agent, no code.

44
00:02:29,323 --> 00:02:31,693
Reset all brings back the values from the code.

45
00:02:32,943 --> 00:02:34,507
Now let's make it fit my phone.

46
00:02:34,507 --> 00:02:38,443
And while we're at it, the screw holes should be countersunk, for wood screws.

47
00:02:38,443 --> 00:02:39,553
I just tell the agent.

48
00:02:40,659 --> 00:02:43,712
The agent changes the sizes and adds the new features.

49
00:02:43,712 --> 00:02:46,709
Then it builds and checks that the phone really fits.

50
00:02:47,559 --> 00:02:47,830
Done.

51
00:02:47,830 --> 00:02:56,009
The stand is now as wide as my phone, the slot at the bottom is 19 millimeters deep for the thick case, and the screw holes at the top are countersunk.

52
00:02:56,959 --> 00:02:57,967
One more idea:

53
00:02:57,967 --> 00:03:00,848
a small tray on the side for my earbuds.

54
00:03:00,848 --> 00:03:04,016
Instead of describing where, I just draw it.

55
00:03:04,016 --> 00:03:06,609
Mark up, a circle, an arrow, a word.

56
00:03:07,309 --> 00:03:09,519
Send it to the agent, and add one sentence.

57
00:03:12,369 --> 00:03:14,419
And there's the tray, right where I drew it.

58
00:03:17,569 --> 00:03:21,619
To compare the two, I ask the agent to put the original next to the new stand.

59
00:03:24,144 --> 00:03:26,013
Side by side, the difference is clear:

60
00:03:26,013 --> 00:03:29,554
the download on the left, and the stand that fits my phone on the right.

61
00:03:31,811 --> 00:03:33,011
Finally, Export.

62
00:03:33,011 --> 00:03:37,061
3MF or STL for your slicer, and you're ready to print.

63
00:03:37,761 --> 00:03:41,811
If you share your remix, credit the original author and keep the same license.

64
00:03:42,711 --> 00:03:47,539
From a download that didn't fit to a part that does, without drawing a single line.

65
00:03:47,539 --> 00:03:49,459
Get SOMA for free at somacad.app.
